  "summary": "A primary air (PA) fan supplies high-pressure air to the coal pulverisers (mills): it dries the coal and carries the fine powder to the burners. It needs much higher pressure than an FD fan at lower flow, so it has a narrow, high-speed impeller; inlet vanes and an outlet damper control and isolate it.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Fan (dynamic) — boiler mill air fan",
    "type": "Centrifugal, narrow high-pressure impeller, IGV + outlet damper"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "blades": 16,
    "pressure": "Typically several times FD fan pressure (plant specific)"
  },
